#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287826 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45901bed-283a-5f6b-a0e8-c82fb99c77cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285423} {:answer/id #uuid "590cea1c-0a7c-5f07-8068-694058c3a868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{44}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285603} {:answer/id #uuid "6649b745-668c-5e5d-b83b-1cf253b1e095" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285716} {:answer/id #uuid "d89e0dd4-5791-5cf7-b3cb-314c7f78a09c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{40}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286760} {:answer/id #uuid "e7904946-6db5-50df-9602-9962763b4fcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{44}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286907}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285716} :answer-field/id #uuid "70430d88-1fa4-5196-ac2c-0e31afc80076" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dc94d59e-a3d1-5387-8338-9ada65b5d11f" :question/math-academy-id "q-18281" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}A=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & =2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-4\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(0+9)-4(0-6)+1(0+2) \\\\  & =18+24+2 \\\\  & =44.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(0-6) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}=\\frac{1}{44}\\cdot 6=\\frac{3}{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287827 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14576e31-28a0-51c9-98e0-cb0e88b08edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284968} {:answer/id #uuid "87d3e443-ddd4-51ad-bc3b-642891265441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286034} {:answer/id #uuid "a41b5f85-604a-5b3f-adf2-0829d0c2aa47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286292} {:answer/id #uuid "b5e84826-763e-57fb-8b0f-9e77c3cef0a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286446} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4a17fa-acb7-5e63-84dc-98fea7d83242" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286492}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286034} :answer-field/id #uuid "12bcbace-edf5-5ef6-b7b6-ab1e80cb8fbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4b297987-b62d-5714-afb9-ac77feefadc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-18282" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ if its determinant is $-2.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(3-0) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21}=\\frac{1}{-2}\\cdot (-3)=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287828 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6942a4fb-bae8-501d-ad2a-66103f54ad63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285753} {:answer/id #uuid "7c6dd01f-de8b-5f99-94f9-eab25a4ecb77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285936} {:answer/id #uuid "82e68463-04bd-50cb-87ed-af0f56c6cae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285988} {:answer/id #uuid "9b48164a-0903-562b-8d03-395f496b0c19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286211} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e18ab7-2363-5919-84cd-f61b850984a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286431}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285753} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ed4da02-e9fd-53f8-937f-fdc5a00e81e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d9f46698-54a7-56c6-b512-47750a5ae9a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-18283" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$ if its determinant is $-4.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =15-(-1) \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31}=\\frac{1}{-4}\\cdot 16=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287829 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20e56ee5-4fb6-5816-869f-e39c23a78b4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285084} {:answer/id #uuid "3fbf79ad-839a-5229-93e9-65fad5cfd1b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285385} {:answer/id #uuid "4eb285a6-7afd-5ad8-ab82-98a513400c25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285520} {:answer/id #uuid "f2cea90f-f0ed-5d57-bca3-334408a81e2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287013} {:answer/id #uuid "fd525363-2a62-5343-aac2-348e4bfefb7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287105}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287105} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac120b1e-d324-518f-9e93-f08acaa655f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "670b2139-910a-54c1-b1cc-9c11eb5fdc1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-18284" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{22}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$ if its determinant is $-16.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{22}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{22}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{22} & =(-1)^{2+2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{22}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{22}=\\frac{1}{-16}\\cdot 4=-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287830 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f415776-37dc-54e3-9800-2d01e510bf06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284919} {:answer/id #uuid "60a2a07e-a39e-5566-8bba-7375b15d76ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285675} {:answer/id #uuid "7595df60-c82c-590b-b868-221b7368f2ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285879} {:answer/id #uuid "a0ab4c0e-9b0e-5237-9348-d4be45093c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286252} {:answer/id #uuid "f133bf14-3c6d-5286-a6d1-bf00852e4721" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287001}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286252} :answer-field/id #uuid "baa7a81a-d6ae-5365-9fa0-1142a694af59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287534}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e5cade28-be41-57ee-910f-46e652127d0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-18285" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & =0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-0+(0-2) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{13} & =(-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-2 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{31}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}=\\frac{1}{-2}\\cdot (-2)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287831 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "232327fd-1dfa-5996-8e84-95bb6a9f8cc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{39}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285103} {:answer/id #uuid "c4f41583-27a2-56ac-9a18-17faf2b31721" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286592} {:answer/id #uuid "c776e656-4613-5245-90ac-bb7e8e9dd6d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286614} {:answer/id #uuid "d31191b1-ed1c-5824-a66f-2602858ec4ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{39}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286707} {:answer/id #uuid "ef342a1d-6164-5836-994c-98cb5484b941" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{39}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286982}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286707} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c346e23-1fbd-5f16-925c-878fb4d2e5f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dcb03ff4-bc8a-5928-846f-20e56388fdb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-18286" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix $A$ $=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ if its determinant is $39.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(-1-0) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23}=\\frac{1}{39}\\cdot 1=\\frac{1}{39}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287832 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06123fff-7c78-51f2-81b7-d35d5c15b5e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284836} {:answer/id #uuid "11d094be-9dc7-5405-8cce-9907e9c51654" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284945} {:answer/id #uuid "3c9cbbbd-12e1-5cce-8786-a3ceed193971" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285356} {:answer/id #uuid "ab1a2f27-2e9e-5b7f-a874-29bebc8a2d4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286347} {:answer/id #uuid "b72dc0b0-3001-5783-b493-cbb1bcd44dc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286459}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284836} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c45b83d-dd3d-58f3-83e0-2b583f24f687" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "35c43087-68b2-5ef3-b590-6196109cdd18" :question/math-academy-id "q-18287" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ if its determinant is $24.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =24-0 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31}=\\frac{1}{24}\\cdot 24=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287833 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2aba01f9-7f51-5a8f-a7a8-dc4fa8fb483a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{71}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285161} {:answer/id #uuid "51897cf6-89ff-547a-a77d-fb4c229f6e36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{71}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285537} {:answer/id #uuid "83757217-5865-5baa-8ad8-1b2c54dde4ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{71}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285995} {:answer/id #uuid "c1f44981-7ac4-5b60-aa71-18f4807ae1be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{71}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286563} {:answer/id #uuid "f5e75515-8616-5fe3-a6a1-8dc2e1fa3a3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{71}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287038}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286563} :answer-field/id #uuid "909dfb56-2abf-58f1-9f5d-3fcdb81ce8b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b862f7e3-dfeb-537e-b5d6-1de6a752faf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-18288" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ if its determinant is $71.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(-3-10) \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}=\\frac{1}{71}\\cdot 13=\\frac{13}{71}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292883 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fba74c9-a43c-555d-83a0-5e97204b4777" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291171}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291171} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea8202f6-c433-5f73-acb4-de5dcc90eb03" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2f93a0ad-99aa-54d9-bd35-c1d6b3dc5f05" :question/math-academy-id "q-275738" :question/problem "If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}x-5 & x+3 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(x-5)\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot (x+3) \\\\  & =-3x+15-2x-6 \\\\  & =-5x+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5x+9 & =0 \\\\ -5x & =-9 \\\\ x & =\\frac{9}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292885 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ed7a213-aacc-56d2-9779-25fff16d3e85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290969}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290969} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7851796-9230-52fb-8a26-b3ea3a329032" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292298}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "30ba35b5-5f35-540d-9096-c30d7199aaa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-275755" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n${a}_{32}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & =3\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+(-3)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(2+2)-0-3(2-0) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}^{t}={c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(6-0) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292886 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0032ffbe-ef0e-59aa-b26f-1bbc10e77544" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290634}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290634} :answer-field/id #uuid "84f92a9c-0b0f-5450-99ed-3b1e0df3d706" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5a90f7ea-2f5b-53dd-b349-fa9148f654dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-275756" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $det(A)=-k.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=-k\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(0+1) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-k)}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ k & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dd1446d-3318-52d7-b8ca-ff5fb69db2c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291032}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291032} :answer-field/id #uuid "e08c8940-8a05-58bf-bed8-cc4535359cbf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292434}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3b033d4e-fbed-55f2-bf1a-00675137d39e" :question/math-academy-id "q-275757" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & -2\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ k & -2\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2+k)-(-4+2)-(2k+2) \\\\  & =2+k+2-2k-2 \\\\  & =2-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}^{t}={c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-k}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{k-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{13}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{k-2} & =-1 \\\\ -1\\cdot (k-2) & =2 \\\\ k-2 & =-2 \\\\ k & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f094e6ec-5f6f-5194-9357-eb5f114fc97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296547}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296547} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a06ad97-49ee-5366-b8f2-4bd5dbd655a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296744} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c475049-0b34-568a-8379-75689981b1cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295611}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295611} :answer-field/id #uuid "58394d53-5ee7-54cb-8c01-d51839d9b8d0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e8e1210d-36f7-5324-a441-3fe5324d9d56" :question/math-academy-id "q-313957" :question/problem "Let $B=\\begin{bmatrix}x-4 & 1 \\\\ 7 & x+2\\end{bmatrix}$\nbe a singular matrix. **In ascending order**, the values of $x$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(x-4)\\cdot (x+2)-7\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-2x-8-7 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-2x-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x-15 & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x-5) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,x=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297543 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "774f2323-67ac-5cdc-be84-7c83c08e1d31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295917}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295917} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a818b40-3c97-5c91-bfcb-9784b9054765" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296716} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "690f3afb-ceb8-5b8e-bb3e-5cad6f4dfb7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295857}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295857} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d4a0345-1cd9-58bc-a954-d45105626bff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296719} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5743304-7d60-5006-a86f-7e14ddb7f705" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296570}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296570} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3a534a3-319d-5a0d-ba11-55a736a3ca56" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5afec83f-c01d-57b0-a129-7a451b173c66" :question/math-academy-id "q-316753" :question/problem "Calculate ${A}^{-1},$ where\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=(-6)\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-5)=3\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -(-5) & -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2/3 & -1 \\\\ 5/3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2/3 & -1 \\\\ 5/3 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2/3 & -1 \\\\ 5/3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297547 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f66079f-8a13-5f2d-b31c-0226934fa120" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295881}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295881} :answer-field/id #uuid "2471fbb6-4020-556f-a24a-22a1c2f5e2a0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296698} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e7b5b59-0ba4-5602-87fc-1603751e6151" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295353}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295353} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d537624-30b3-5cb7-b8f0-e8594a47571a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296889} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64863451-c3cd-5629-ac5b-993b0bd3afb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295839}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295839} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1ddbf64-a9bc-5822-9543-9eb5227576a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1c5d479a-db20-5ea3-ab0e-6622e81ae62c" :question/math-academy-id "q-316768" :question/problem "Calculate ${A}^{-1},$ where\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=5\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 0=-10\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-10}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1/5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1/2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1/5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1/2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1/5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1/2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299499 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ff1b0a9-fde2-5367-87f0-bb860645334c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298176}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298176} :answer-field/id #uuid "588ee9fc-b1ad-590a-902a-aa67ff051060" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298940} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e235848-7d84-5c03-8f30-0fd2297b7d8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297879}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297879} :answer-field/id #uuid "98cadb3e-fd34-5d08-9dd7-982a5a1572bf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299143} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a55fb1b2-3b16-5c94-9d74-cc1c7a144fb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298278}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298278} :answer-field/id #uuid "e519f8fb-61e9-5c0d-a5e4-7091ce4b87b3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2eafafcb-8727-5ab6-b75d-030156359000" :question/math-academy-id "q-316780" :question/problem "Calculate ${A}^{-1},$ where\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=6\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 9=-12\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-12}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1/12 & 1/6 \\\\ 3/4 & -1/2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1/12 & 1/6 \\\\ 3/4 & -1/2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1/12 & 1/6 \\\\ 3/4 & -1/2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299500 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b2c8819-78f4-5fff-bc17-cec5c19efd38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298086}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298086} :answer-field/id #uuid "b790ef95-1954-53e9-951c-93434ba44d92" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299257}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "95d2a0a0-79cd-50d5-95db-d0f4cfda76fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-316781" :question/problem "If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}2x & 5x-1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(2x)\\cdot (-2)-4\\cdot (5x-1) \\\\  & =-4x+4-20x \\\\  & =-24x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-24x+4 & =0 \\\\ 24x & =4 \\\\ x & =\\frac{4}{24} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299501 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "892579b6-7828-5a0d-ab85-d5b77ff9a388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298147}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298147} :answer-field/id #uuid "e05f6368-cb27-51a1-9aa0-8c61326772fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299398}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0e69fc32-4426-5cb8-9829-2fc1f8cd28fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-316782" :question/problem "If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3x+2 & 2x-4\\end{bmatrix}$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =1\\cdot (2x-4)-2\\cdot (3x+2) \\\\  & =2x-4-6x-4 \\\\  & =-4x-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x-8 & =0 \\\\ -4x & =8 \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299502 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f65bbf81-a8fe-5107-aa3e-22d11d717c75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298604}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298604} :answer-field/id #uuid "635dc510-988f-5cfd-b2b9-b02500ed4e94" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a90dc1ce-cf3a-57f1-9a32-63fe824c4a01" :question/math-academy-id "q-316783" :question/problem "If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}5x & -1 \\\\ 6x-8 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(5x)\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (6x-8) \\\\  & =10x+6x-8 \\\\  & =16x-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16x-8 & =0 \\\\ 16x & =8 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299503 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c35d1a75-f277-5a94-961c-420517cab2dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298410}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298410} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ee21428-abe9-5f94-b753-8373c581c767" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1bc74342-0f37-5e04-9085-a552735d6bba" :question/math-academy-id "q-316784" :question/problem "If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -x+1 \\\\ 5 & 2x+7\\end{bmatrix}$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(-3)\\cdot (2x+7)-5\\cdot (-x+1) \\\\  & =-6x-21+5x-5 \\\\  & =-x-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x-26 & =0 \\\\ -x & =26 \\\\ x & =-26\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299504 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04cca41b-96b6-5473-9aca-86b0db2b84ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297576}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297576} :answer-field/id #uuid "32d3dd1b-e2db-5caf-ae0b-809e4a9c8547" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6d52bc53-4740-5cbf-85a5-c4eda2c297f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-316785" :question/problem "If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 7x-3 & x+8\\end{bmatrix}$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =4\\cdot (x+8)-(-2)\\cdot (7x-3) \\\\  & =4x+32+14x-6 \\\\  & =18x+26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18x+26 & =0 \\\\ 18x & =-26 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{13}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299506 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "629ba2fb-f7a0-55ec-8318-3a578b3a696d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297974}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297974} :answer-field/id #uuid "0facb49d-44d7-596b-8283-cf6ecd88d19e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298692} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b84a7230-bf17-5af7-b714-634c6fe7a61b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298353}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298353} :answer-field/id #uuid "2558d65a-fb7e-502b-9124-c77726154021" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "113042b9-3913-565d-9ff6-26aa252c490f" :question/math-academy-id "q-316825" :question/problem "Let $B=\\begin{bmatrix}2x+4 & 0 \\\\ 15 & -x-3\\end{bmatrix}$\nbe a singular matrix. **In ascending order**, the values of $x$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(2x+4)\\cdot (-x-3)-0\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-6x-4x-12 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-10x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-10x-12 & =0 \\\\ -2({x}^{2}+5x+6) & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,x=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299507 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5366c8ee-0f20-52a8-af0d-6262c3e3a64d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297903}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297903} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d33276a-59ca-5611-8a71-d122c8fe1aa8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298680} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08d68a03-e244-5376-9981-66b7a4ebd931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297599}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297599} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ef19e34-416f-58ea-9adf-3a70138385ab" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298743}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5a81a924-c8d9-5da7-9d7c-338e9d3bb52d" :question/math-academy-id "q-316828" :question/problem "Let $B=\\begin{bmatrix}2x+1 & x-40 \\\\ 1 & -x\\end{bmatrix}$\nbe a singular matrix. **In ascending order**, the values of $x$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(2x+1)\\cdot (-x)-(x-40)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-x-x+40 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-2x+40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-2x+40 & =0 \\\\ -2({x}^{2}+x-20) & =0 \\\\ -2(x-4)(x+5) & =0 \\\\ x & =4,-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=-5\\,\\text{and}\\,x=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299508 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd68271a-9473-595e-b5cc-3fdbfc5ed8a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298378}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298378} :answer-field/id #uuid "91c07df3-718b-531d-bfd7-b454f78a656b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299118} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ab82d06-28db-5541-b1f2-29ddc998b877" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297608}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297608} :answer-field/id #uuid "e11d6092-7929-53ab-a1f3-28dc7122ce6a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299403}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e6886658-7f8f-54c1-b88e-4ea7a22c6205" :question/math-academy-id "q-316829" :question/problem "Let $B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -x+7 \\\\ x-5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nbe a singular matrix. **In ascending order**, the values of $x$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =3\\cdot 0-(-x+7)\\cdot (x-5) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-5x-7x+35 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-12x+35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-12x+35 & =0 \\\\ (x-7)(x-5) & =0 \\\\ x & =7,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=5\\,\\text{and}\\,x=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299747 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4f2334d-4d19-5657-ae3e-4861480ed63d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298594}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298594} :answer-field/id #uuid "78b9513e-697d-5d7b-bee1-be7a3d121ec8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299048} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bbfc66b-fff8-5004-b6dd-86427e259c6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297674}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297674} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0d77a70-66b2-5ffc-82b6-2ce4bec2f8bb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299237} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90e59730-fbc2-5bbb-83ce-1f84517628d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298183}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298183} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9818ff9-bf1d-504a-a640-f403039467ce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0876fd99-09ab-5402-abb3-c07e19b050b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-319360" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=-5.$\n\n|  |  | $-17$ | {{field-1}} | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\,$ |  | $12$ | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |\n|  |  | $-3$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-17 & -12 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-17 & 12 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-17 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-17 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299749 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b1e8767-de2d-52c7-8e2b-c1d59dee9c2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298230}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298230} :answer-field/id #uuid "083d9e98-ca8d-5676-958b-ffeedf627de1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298664} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1899ba9d-d3c7-55ce-9eb0-e8c2dc7a4673" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297659}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297659} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e3ce860-5116-5e9b-8117-529c03e68d73" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298901} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5975fdb6-cb9e-539a-b015-6e5266540e3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297926}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297926} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8b9f6c6-8575-50de-8fb6-95b3ce4f2904" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "228d219f-a988-51e3-add6-8253de28fd6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-319370" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=-4.$\n\n|  |  | $-1$ | {{field-1}} | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\,$ |  | $4$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  |\n|  |  | $7$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 9 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 9 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299750 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a46a2082-4701-5caa-8a18-53b0c4269a8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298274}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298274} :answer-field/id #uuid "598ac1fb-ed3b-5180-8cb1-1204c40529bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298943} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66ae1504-4970-5613-87dc-94b7c840f849" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297990}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297990} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e4160be-bab1-5130-a5b3-baad952ec2d9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299062} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd4225cd-a6f9-5811-a080-99edbbbc07c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298445}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298445} :answer-field/id #uuid "b02672dc-f7e5-58dc-a2a8-072fe03a302b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299233}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "74394102-8729-5a30-8d7e-62d8f0117047" :question/math-academy-id "q-319372" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=7.$\n\n|  |  | $-1$ | {{field-1}} | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\,$ |  | $-11$ | {{field-2}} | $3$ |  |\n|  |  | $-4$ | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 11 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -11 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -10 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -11 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -11 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299753 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9aca02af-1267-5495-8514-3c0b3c60eb1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298229}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298229} :answer-field/id #uuid "334b73ec-67fc-5e0a-a799-7aa8a5b37cd6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298812} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43320049-f27b-50cd-97bc-171b22e5c4c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297824}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297824} :answer-field/id #uuid "78f99d59-45ab-5371-902e-8352a898486d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299049} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e895a78-e9aa-58ba-aab5-2fa17cb12e1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297950}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297950} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b9d8fad-aa30-5871-84b3-b6f919b19455" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49aed189-4a5b-58cc-bc59-cee854ce956e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297854}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297854} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ece9237-745d-5b97-a4df-453863812eaa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ca1a8117-1d26-5acd-beac-beb6e4c1cfa3" :question/math-academy-id "q-319395" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n|  |  | $-1$ | $-3$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ {{field-2}} |  | $-1$ | $3$ | {{field-3}} |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | $3$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & =(-3)\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3)(2-3)-0(\\,-2-(-3)\\,)+(-3+3) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299754 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6598caed-bd43-5485-82fc-6172d6afee81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2/11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297986}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297986} :answer-field/id #uuid "87b160ba-8853-58cf-97da-7d8ad0eb9b07" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299093}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e7e72b45-0695-5b36-9476-7542514f8aaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-319409" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n${a}_{32}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{vmatrix} & =2\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(6-0)-0(-3-0)-1(1-0) \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}^{t}={c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(2-0) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299756 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4ed675a-e374-5734-95e6-b38d1d46a8c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298339}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298339} :answer-field/id #uuid "9144a26f-d207-5329-a4f2-7e4b73ff0242" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e9cc9cf4-3e2c-5fa2-9cc3-9a41fb5db658" :question/math-academy-id "q-319413" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n${a}_{12}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & =2\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(6-0)-0(-2-0)-1(1-0) \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(0+1) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299757 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08bb5b15-8035-5a87-b994-7a63a290fd15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5/13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297598}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297598} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a8cea55-04b6-5a91-988e-863b5a98418a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8dd1f6d6-3609-5dae-86b5-57186f677ef3" :question/math-academy-id "q-319416" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n${a}_{33}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(2-(-3))+2(4-0)+0(6-0) \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{33}^{t}={c}_{33}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{33} & =(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =+\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1+4) \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{33}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{33}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{33} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299758 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca3eaad9-1dc3-55cb-ab62-7139f24f233d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298432}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298432} :answer-field/id #uuid "fef19aba-acb5-5246-8048-25a4732b0153" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d6120ca6-9e08-5dd7-8756-664c0b14c937" :question/math-academy-id "q-319420" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n${a}_{31}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\,(2+1)-0\\,(0-1)+2\\,(-0-2) \\\\  & =3-0-4 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}^{t}={c}_{13}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{13} & =(-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =+\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-0 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{31}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299761 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a25d310-05ab-55e4-a1c5-609bfd85c0b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297780}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297780} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a79b5b0-3b96-5509-bde8-4a7499f7d418" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298732}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b74699a3-68fd-5996-962f-7d078766e370" :question/math-academy-id "q-319434" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $\\frac{1}{3}$ and $det(A)=1-2k.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=1-2k\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(1\\cdot k-0\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1-2k)}\\cdot (-k) \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{\\,2k-1\\,}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=\\frac{1}{3}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{\\,2k-1\\,} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 3k & =2k-1 \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299762 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6821836-cff5-597c-bfe8-284e273211b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298473}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298473} :answer-field/id #uuid "5334a997-fbd8-5492-a178-58a2c8133561" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d4e42e14-a47f-5067-a3e2-ccca26a8935c" :question/math-academy-id "q-319437" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $\\frac{1}{2}$ and $det(A)=k-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=k-1\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}^{t}={c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(-1+2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-1}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{k-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{23}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{k-1} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ k-1 & =-2 \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299764 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19779c74-033c-527e-8527-75fcd9cd52be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9/2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297661}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297661} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a13f4b6-0d0b-5ddd-bc05-cb3e7f407353" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f7cdf079-0dbd-550b-985e-14ed1ec133fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-319442" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $\\frac{1}{4}$ and $det(A)=-2k-3.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=-2k-3\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}^{t}={c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(1+2) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2k-3)}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\,2k+3\\,}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{23}^{′}=\\frac{1}{4}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\,2k+3\\,} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 12 & =2k+3 \\\\ 2k & =9 \\\\ k & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299765 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9efe1417-3245-50a4-a08e-1226edd401f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2/3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298255}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298255} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2fd473d-2b44-5cd3-afbc-189ab115bc74" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299452}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "24df41a5-9c85-5f3d-b3b0-277ec8e095a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-319443" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & k & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $det(A)=k-2.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=k-2\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}^{t}={c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}\\begin{vmatrix}k & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}k & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =k+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(k-2)}\\cdot (k+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{k+2}{\\,k-2\\,}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{13}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k+2}{\\,k-2\\,} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2(k+2) & =-(k-2) \\\\ 2k+4 & =-k+2 \\\\ 3k & =-2 \\\\ k & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299776 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67507fa1-9c8b-533b-b35f-b2b75970e742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297996}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297996} :answer-field/id #uuid "86f29c10-686e-51f4-8830-5217f4abdf63" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2b5cf762-3178-5e63-a1b0-8da0e65dccf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-319546" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nif its determinant is $17.$\n\n${a}_{13}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\,1\\cdot (1\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\,{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299777 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30fc4049-b346-5ef3-b721-8b7b6804b08f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297759}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297759} :answer-field/id #uuid "83e9901e-f892-512e-a362-56ac30375949" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "66b7eb82-0c6f-5154-a5bd-434c9571ba55" :question/math-academy-id "q-319549" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nif its determinant is $3.$\n\n${a}_{21}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\,(1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\,{c}_{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299778 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c573351-ee99-56f5-889f-894b79759197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298090}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298090} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e78f910-eafd-5dde-95e7-840e8bbf0359" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "959ebdb0-727b-5193-9194-4f73c8f717da" :question/math-academy-id "q-319550" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nif its determinant is $-22.$\n\n${a}_{33}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{33}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{33} & =(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\,1\\cdot (2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{33}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\,{c}_{33} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-22}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299801 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f879e289-265f-50e1-93a8-bc1f3228e612" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298611}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298611} :answer-field/id #uuid "66a8d0a5-264a-526a-bf26-7c2ead18114a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "dc09a39f-9bc3-5b8d-97b8-ec01ec4b162d" :question/math-academy-id "q-319859" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ k & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nequals $-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ k & -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}=1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ k & 2\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ k & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\,(1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))-2\\,(0\\cdot 2-1\\cdot k)+(-1)\\,(0\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot k) \\\\  & =(2+1)-2\\,(-k)+(-1)\\,(-k) \\\\  & =3+2k+k \\\\  & =3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-(4-1) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3k+3}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{3k+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2}$, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-3}{3k+3} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -3k-3 & =-6 \\\\ -3k & =-6+3 \\\\ k & =\\frac{-3}{-3} \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299809 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbeaf4d4-0e00-520e-99d0-3bee5b93deca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298438}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298438} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcfa3e0a-bb95-5124-94ff-faa0c2a5654f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7aba959b-00b2-5aea-a09a-80fa0c6d7e58" :question/math-academy-id "q-319937" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & k & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nequals $-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & k & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ k & -2\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(1\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot k)+(0\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot 3)+(0\\cdot k-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =2(k-2)+3-3 \\\\  & =2k-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}^{t}={c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(2\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-(-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{23}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2k-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{23}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k-2} & =-1 \\\\ 1 & =-(k-2) \\\\ k-2 & =-1 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299812 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00f85809-939f-5696-b20f-6a24d1b3a8b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297553}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297553} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c533b51-00bb-5918-948d-af70d14f79e3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "44f3f3e2-3340-514f-8bf3-b71afd4ac18e" :question/math-academy-id "q-319944" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ k & -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nequals $-2.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ k & -2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ k & -1\\end{vmatrix}+(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ k & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-2)((-1)(-1)-(-2)(-2))+2((-2)(-1)-(-2)k)+(-2)((-2)(-2)-(-1)k) \\\\  & =(-2)(1-4)+2(2+2k)+(-2)(4+k) \\\\  & =6+4+4k-8-2k \\\\  & =2k+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}^{t}={c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ k & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-((-2)(-2)-(-2)k) \\\\  & =-(4+2k) \\\\  & =-2k-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{32}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2k-4}{2k+2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{k+2}{k+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{32}^{′}=-2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{k+2}{k+1} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{k+2}{k+1} & =2 \\\\ k+2 & =2k+2 \\\\ k & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bec7eef-98ab-50a1-a827-b84e71a0b5c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300251} {:answer/id #uuid "3f84bdbb-e043-5047-a36e-5da69a5c79e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300274} {:answer/id #uuid "48bd8464-99de-5369-8e7b-9fe677ea1700" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300331} {:answer/id #uuid "a04b15ad-a1bc-5b8c-b98c-a273e45d97d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300771} {:answer/id #uuid "a93e42c1-d25f-5c74-aa8c-ac931bf2b4fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300810}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300251} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf01f982-1095-5239-a807-cfb6858ba6e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f43456bf-f295-5e3b-a9b3-15b153a5e800" :question/math-academy-id "q-32727" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle S=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & ={s}_{11}{C}_{11}+{s}_{12}{C}_{12}+{s}_{13}{C}_{13}+{s}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+2\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =2{C}_{12} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}∗ & 2 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ 1 & ∗ & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & ∗ & -5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & ∗ & 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-2\\left(1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =-2((-5\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 2)-0+0) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-18) \\\\  & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302372 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0abde6ff-968f-5c10-a57e-e9337ccb9853" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-198" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299986} {:answer/id #uuid "0c0b0e8c-b5e8-5d1a-8a64-83154e74252f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299995} {:answer/id #uuid "1824105f-b810-5b30-a0aa-0beb57bd268f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300062} {:answer/id #uuid "6e3832ab-4326-5da4-9681-13c8424ca43e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300518} {:answer/id #uuid "b97de0dc-d8bc-5f26-9307-169bdbb2d021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-432" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300890}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300890} :answer-field/id #uuid "54890664-57f3-5254-b119-6383b3902222" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8643e81c-8c77-5255-a120-2681f124c049" :question/math-academy-id "q-32791" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle T=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 6 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & ={t}_{11}{C}_{11}+{t}_{12}{C}_{12}+{t}_{13}{C}_{13}+{t}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+4\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =-{C}_{11}+4{C}_{13} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 6 & 0 & 2 \\\\ ∗ & 0 & 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+4\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}∗ & ∗ & 4 & ∗ \\\\ 9 & 0 & ∗ & 0 \\\\ -1 & 6 & ∗ & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & ∗ & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+4\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\\right)+4\\left(9\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =-0+4\\cdot 9(6\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =36\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =-432\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302373 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a74fc00-fd64-5b42-9d9b-22c961b3e9a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}7 & -3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 8 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -9 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300080} {:answer/id #uuid "456f14d2-c05d-5f77-a95f-02402a88764b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 8 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300308} {:answer/id #uuid "d80443ba-23ec-52cf-8364-fc8db3ddda93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 8 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301037} {:answer/id #uuid "e535d5d8-1a5b-50ea-bcd5-0d5de112cc6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 8 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 10\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301098} {:answer/id #uuid "ea6110fe-7888-57df-94d3-e8bd05499930" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 8 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 10\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301122}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301098} :answer-field/id #uuid "387a8cf8-7099-56dd-8883-b322ddd9523b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301410}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7ce9f7cf-7221-5005-8e3f-a5d9b8f1addd" :question/math-academy-id "q-32793" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of ${d}_{15}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & -3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 10 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, to get the minor of ${d}_{15}$, we remove the $1$st row and $5$th column: \n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & 2 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 0 & ∗ \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & 4 & ∗ \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 1 & ∗ \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 10 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n \nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{15}=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 8 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 10\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cofactor of ${d}_{15}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{15} & =(-1)^{1+5}{M}_{15} \\\\  & ={M}_{15} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 8 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 10\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323744 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "147888b7-3be1-5c61-a527-09bd238c54f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321314} {:answer/id #uuid "57a12085-d4fa-57ec-8059-de705274f776" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321836} {:answer/id #uuid "8f51fed1-08a6-55a3-a261-1c9416d371f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322285} {:answer/id #uuid "ab001798-4c95-52c6-8bb5-a0283265953d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322489} {:answer/id #uuid "de5ed94a-712c-5cd7-b285-0cdfce1efa19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322884}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186322489} :answer-field/id #uuid "910c107e-8209-55ad-aaee-2dfef20df5ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323452}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9ae55842-6a04-591a-82b0-c1e71e70c4a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-36043" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of ${b}_{34}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, to get the minor of ${b}_{34}$, we remove the $3$rd row and the $4$th column: \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 3 & ∗ \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & -2 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 0 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{34}=\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cofactor of ${b}_{34}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{34} & =(-1)^{3+4}{M}_{34} \\\\  & =-{M}_{34} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323745 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e995287-b0ce-5d14-adf9-a8c9c41bfbc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321381} {:answer/id #uuid "2135e8a8-7aa1-5be7-a729-d18fff9337df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321397} {:answer/id #uuid "23cebe08-003e-58dd-b604-3b895669fb51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321421} {:answer/id #uuid "30a88961-6b47-51d0-bc38-90b444ad5cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-62" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321521} {:answer/id #uuid "ec560ecf-e9c3-5994-aee2-a1534c401d48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323004}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321521} :answer-field/id #uuid "9029e3eb-d47c-517f-8e68-1e0ac69f0975" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5505f107-cfef-57b0-b433-16953d2d1848" :question/math-academy-id "q-36045" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle Z=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Z) & ={z}_{11}{C}_{11}+{z}_{12}{C}_{12}+{z}_{13}{C}_{13}+{z}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =1\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & ={C}_{11}-{C}_{13} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & -3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ ∗ & 4 & 3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}∗ & ∗ & -1 & ∗ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ∗ & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & ∗ & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\\right)-\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =0+2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+0-(0-0+0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2((-3)\\cdot 5-4\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-31) \\\\  & =-62\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323746 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c5244df-f0a9-5c2e-a73e-51aa0a825ac6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-178" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321614} {:answer/id #uuid "4c8e0c45-d2b6-5efa-8628-e01af954659c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "148" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321750} {:answer/id #uuid "52dec254-4e05-5958-b362-9315402fc410" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-371" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321800} {:answer/id #uuid "db1797e4-6de8-5d10-b3fb-c58f8e24e85f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "315" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322864} {:answer/id #uuid "f5e68f5c-b2e0-51fc-9ac1-cb001e6b3caa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "157" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323074}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321750} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f090c82-dafa-5202-866e-f37a38c4880e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "59bec8fd-d214-5893-9146-596b7aabe9e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-36053" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle U=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & ={u}_{11}{C}_{11}+{u}_{12}{C}_{12}+{u}_{13}{C}_{13}+{u}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =5\\cdot {C}_{11}+(-2)\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =5{C}_{11}-2{C}_{12} \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}5 & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 6 & 0 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & 2 & 5 & -4\\end{vmatrix}+(-2)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}∗ & -2 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗ & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & ∗ & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & ∗ & 5 & -4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -4\\end{vmatrix}+(-2)\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =5\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -4\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =5\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{vmatrix}-1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\\right)+2\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{vmatrix}-1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =5(0-(6\\cdot (-4)-1\\cdot 2)+0)+2(0-(3\\cdot (-4)-1\\cdot (-3))+0) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 26+2\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =130+18 \\\\  & =148\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326843 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f00af2-b840-5786-b28b-1f6973830285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324045} {:answer/id #uuid "b0650f26-5533-5b0a-9347-28807009e5c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325475} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e20584-c42b-540c-abb4-0d75908bf38f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325812} {:answer/id #uuid "e0878097-34b5-589b-a86b-0981c9097b18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325933} {:answer/id #uuid "fde0d5e3-6d10-584d-a825-0b58e5e1d31b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-5 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326210}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324045} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec36ae3f-3647-5b17-9422-159a73ac8d97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ed7ec0b2-f754-51c2-b65a-169d7f4dad10" :question/math-academy-id "q-40449" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of ${a}_{13}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -2 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, to get the minor of ${a}_{13}$,  we remove the $1$st row and the $3$rd column:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{vmatrix}∗ & ∗ & 1 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & 2 & ∗ & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 7 & ∗ & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -5 & ∗ & 1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & ∗ & 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{13}=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cofactor of ${a}_{13}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{13} & =(-1)^{1+3}{M}_{13} \\\\  & ={M}_{13} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339016 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fd7bbbf-6e0c-51c5-a9fa-fc0f2bf1d945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467896} {:answer/id #uuid "c58e8001-ca94-52dc-9ac3-efcb68b4cfa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467897}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467897} :answer-field/id #uuid "0afb67d1-8168-5df5-930f-8190b07edc62" :answer-field/key "$R=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468669} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6fa4bf8-f217-5274-8dab-28c162bb278d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467898} {:answer/id #uuid "f93fd016-1442-53ad-8597-12bc1e59568b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467899}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467899} :answer-field/id #uuid "a00bd3e1-111e-5780-871b-467da013e81a" :answer-field/key "$S=\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468670} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f78fc2c-5319-559a-b65c-0b1064d9bbc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467900} {:answer/id #uuid "906cb48c-7d29-5136-a248-2c29457a1fee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467901}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467900} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4c5cafc-4559-5564-a3f4-1bb51c7edb62" :answer-field/key "$T=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6118feb2-c751-599a-b3b9-c8c760c49b6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-71934" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $R$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(R)=5\\cdot 4-10\\cdot 2=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(R)=0,$ we conclude that $R$ is not invertible.\n\n- The matrix $S$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(T)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $T$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $R$ and $S$ do not have an inverse."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339017 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b04e9358-9109-5802-a83d-c003136f6776" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467902} {:answer/id #uuid "711d5a0b-0232-5cb7-8a88-a13f69141094" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467903}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467903} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b39826b-4d43-597b-b35d-5dd3a91ceaf8" :answer-field/key "$X=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 6 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468672} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af6e952f-1b3d-5415-9986-1f855a35a9dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467904} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a6c71b-66a8-52d7-88ab-87e3a0607923" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467905}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467904} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f838e05-1a03-57ee-8f9c-10a9e960bcdd" :answer-field/key "$Y=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468673} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e98450e-f707-5f45-880a-72823035ac85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467906} {:answer/id #uuid "3b62048c-e540-5983-8cbf-aabcf18ff59a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467907}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467906} :answer-field/id #uuid "2386ffd6-0069-5a17-ae65-0bf5f760c977" :answer-field/key "$Z=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f09c20fa-fbe3-5a9f-8218-d2a4dd2af13c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71938" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $X$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Y$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Y)=6\\cdot 6-7\\cdot 5=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Y)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Y$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Z$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=(-2)\\cdot 5-10\\cdot 1=-20.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Z)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Z$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $X$ does not have an inverse."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339028 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16f0d1eb-63da-516d-b39c-98936ea702c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336248} {:answer/id #uuid "3e475449-d5a0-5355-9040-0c60f6ed7506" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336619} {:answer/id #uuid "4b8e773e-5ecc-5ed1-a6ae-65cce087450b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336734} {:answer/id #uuid "94bf4718-c6d0-59d1-9ec4-b22670dd22eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337391} {:answer/id #uuid "96bb9ff0-d964-5085-8a7c-e0e55abb0c09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337403}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337403} :answer-field/id #uuid "01585e92-cf9f-5695-8971-52db4143edc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1f42b909-72e3-5c68-a789-fc35f80e300c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71967" :question/problem "If $V=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & y \\\\ 5 & y\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $V$ is singular if and only if $det(V)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(V) & =7\\cdot y-5\\cdot y \\\\  & =7y-5y \\\\  & =2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $y$ is $y=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339029 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1608f206-6cae-571f-8d1e-16b6d162d46d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=\\pm 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336238} {:answer/id #uuid "287ca0dc-331e-527d-b8c0-e766a590d0c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=\\pm 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336411} {:answer/id #uuid "8f1fd271-6941-56e0-8167-86c17416a68a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337323} {:answer/id #uuid "9f6e027a-7384-58dc-b2bb-94433e7f22eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337473} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f32404-27a9-5015-979f-c6987e1fe3c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338010}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336411} :answer-field/id #uuid "53c72237-b3c8-5418-adbd-d5b4558f878e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d71eb817-7b8e-5d55-9dca-4bfa26de23cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-71968" :question/problem "If $H=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & c \\\\ c & 5\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $H$ is singular if and only if $det(H)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(H) & =5\\cdot 5-c\\cdot c \\\\  & =25-{c}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25-{c}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =25 \\\\ c & =\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $c$ are $c=\\pm 5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339030 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f062ffd-0731-5c9d-b5df-1e280483ad62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336623} {:answer/id #uuid "87e8b87b-9219-5612-bc47-0727af4eb0b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337259} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1a9b12-eb65-52f2-be17-471977096571" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337454} {:answer/id #uuid "db1521d6-6365-5c27-8635-662375c34db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337942} {:answer/id #uuid "e0112779-824d-50fa-a23d-b42b80a0e397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337989}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337259} :answer-field/id #uuid "82b667e3-83f0-533b-abd1-94355475f197" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338510}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "35c7dc25-96f0-5d9f-9d6a-dfbf5fcfb320" :question/math-academy-id "q-71969" :question/problem "If $M=\\begin{bmatrix}t & 4 \\\\ t & 10\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot 10-t\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =10t-4t \\\\  & =6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342006 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "444cd60d-98f8-57c7-9875-93fe9bccf0fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339729} {:answer/id #uuid "534e79d6-1a48-52d9-8361-6b5e12a9cdf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339897} {:answer/id #uuid "53b60466-c23f-5e4c-9676-8a33e27c13b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339902} {:answer/id #uuid "87d00cf2-3923-56f4-a41d-5b87aa3fb375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340345} {:answer/id #uuid "da2aff30-bbeb-5d42-9525-3fe5517ebd88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341064}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341064} :answer-field/id #uuid "45ff8668-6658-5885-8426-f8efdc154b15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4a069e33-ab79-5e52-8347-ee8dc3251c92" :question/math-academy-id "q-73535" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & k \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $\\frac{1}{4}$ and $det(A)=6+3k.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=6+3k\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{33}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{33} & =(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2-(-1) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{33}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{33} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6+3k}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2+k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{33}^{′}=\\frac{1}{4}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{1}{2+k} \\\\ 2+k & =4 \\\\ k & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "665c812a-56dd-5bc5-b0c8-ffde25e8fa1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340028} {:answer/id #uuid "ae5fface-39c3-5bf8-a1ce-22c8363e23e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340717} {:answer/id #uuid "b15c3399-c900-542c-998e-a75077eccf14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340742} {:answer/id #uuid "c27c70d1-a640-5ece-ae8a-27b55a8741af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340859} {:answer/id #uuid "e7fa4eea-3361-5d16-9459-3c3594fb683d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341175}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340028} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aa240fd-e96d-535e-8b4a-f32a7de1ce5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "33a7f588-04f8-5fc0-9705-3e73eb1453a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-73542" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ k & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $1.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ k & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}k & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\begin{vmatrix}k & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-2-0)+(-2k-0)+0 \\\\  & =-2k-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(1-(-3)) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k-2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{k+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{32}^{′}=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{k+1} & =1 \\\\ 2 & =k+1 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342009 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05beee91-a392-5f65-88d2-f7fc95e409b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339177} {:answer/id #uuid "817291a6-cca7-53a6-bdbd-a95cc30beb48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340293} {:answer/id #uuid "98547d62-efa4-543b-b561-835c71d9986d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340498} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1fa043-012b-58dc-8eb3-9d118befac20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340804} {:answer/id #uuid "e51c2424-ac45-594a-b4be-5f0fea419df3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341155}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341155} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c974da0-7d8a-5c4f-9610-badc09e2e785" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341544}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "93b0be09-4ca6-5085-9855-e90445a7accc" :question/math-academy-id "q-73545" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{11}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & k\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $\\frac{4}{5}.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & k\\end{vmatrix} & =2\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix}+0\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(-k-6)-(0-3) \\\\  & =-2k-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{11}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{11}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{11} & =(-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-k-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{11} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k-9}\\cdot (-k-6) \\\\  & =\\frac{k+6}{2k+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{11}^{′}=\\frac{4}{5}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k+6}{2k+9} & =\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ 5(k+6) & =4(2k+9) \\\\ 5k+30 & =8k+36 \\\\ 3k & =-6 \\\\ k & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348176 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b8bcb10-ac3e-55b6-b031-7dbf74e239f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345737} {:answer/id #uuid "59fd8952-62da-5a67-b9f7-07fe0e852847" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346119} {:answer/id #uuid "d49fb2b3-f414-5e50-a37a-0e6179c2bd77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347218} {:answer/id #uuid "ed42e7fe-6e5f-52f5-bd0b-40cd218c7c42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 8 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347444} {:answer/id #uuid "f42a5c98-7204-58b2-97fa-48ee5b75bef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347516}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347218} :answer-field/id #uuid "259e0501-a96f-5581-b7ba-bcbbab78467e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d05fea71-6716-5388-8215-29b86b42d217" :question/math-academy-id "q-7921" :question/problem "Calculate ${E}^{-1}$, where\n$$\n\\displaystyle E=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $E$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(E)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(E)=4\\cdot 7-8\\cdot 3=4\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(E)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E{E}^{-1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {E}^{-1}E & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348182 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20dd891b-d694-5499-8817-937a44eceff4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468238} {:answer/id #uuid "d5955946-ccfb-5755-8612-e0cdabb5eab7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468239}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468238} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a54a548-43f3-5af9-bb27-c37157e1ba17" :answer-field/key "$D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468840} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91fda060-34cb-56bf-a286-798cf5974bde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468240} {:answer/id #uuid "691d2f9b-6944-52d3-b95e-6577e5ed9262" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468241}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468241} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1dfcd78-f8c3-5201-b805-25717f44d7c0" :answer-field/key "$F=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468841} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44aed856-5960-53b9-88e1-18229b5f5d72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468242} {:answer/id #uuid "cbda35bc-2510-530d-8b17-8fd2a72ea3be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468243}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468242} :answer-field/id #uuid "121ad5e6-2d71-5c46-b7a0-42914d3db890" :answer-field/key "$G=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6cd97c58-6193-5fe7-8948-41d6f4bfcd71" :question/math-academy-id "q-7923" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $D$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(D)=3\\cdot 6-6\\cdot 2=6.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(D)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $D$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $F$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(F)=6\\cdot 6-6\\cdot 6=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(F)=0,$ we conclude that $F$ is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $G$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(G)=(-2)\\cdot 4-4\\cdot 2=-16.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(G)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $G$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $F$ does not have an inverse."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362383 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "742aed52-3923-5d3e-aae7-5ca575086d97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -10 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361349} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad587c3-4f5c-5eca-b96d-64e234660df7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361450} {:answer/id #uuid "a4c8cb0e-1acd-5b83-85e0-b9b1a7bde4b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361575} {:answer/id #uuid "caa1fb09-e645-5bb3-bc36-d3b843dcd6d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 9 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361752} {:answer/id #uuid "e206a94e-4884-53b0-b2c6-1a2394ba3c14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -10 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361847}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186361575} :answer-field/id #uuid "240210d3-d2e3-5a83-9c97-d93c03a1d0de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362012}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7e033a7c-c230-5700-a5b4-d8c955024d86" :question/math-academy-id "q-9967" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & =4\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4(-12+10)+2(32-35)+3(-16+21) \\\\  & =-8-6+15 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
